# Frontend Standards

Frontend work must follow the Spec Registry:

- `specs/README.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-001-security-baseline.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-002-security-testing.md`

Mandatory frontend expectations:

- preserve approved UX unless the active spec explicitly changes it;
- keep routes, module naming and folder structure aligned with the registry;
- never expose secrets, API keys, tokens or private endpoints in client bundles;
- avoid raw HTML rendering; sanitize any HTML or Markdown before display;
- use `rel="noopener noreferrer"` for external links opened in new tabs;
- do not store JWT access tokens in `localStorage` unless a security spec explicitly approves it;
- keep production sourcemaps private or disabled;
- add tests for meaningful UI behavior, routing, permissions and security-sensitive rendering.
